msgid "内存与资源生命周期"
msgstr "Memory and resource lifecycles"

msgid "地址空间"
msgstr "Address spaces"

msgid ""
"页表、物理页、堆和用户内存访问分别由 arch/x86_64/mm 与 mm 子目录负责。 用户指针操作检查范围、权限、长度及目标页表，不能用当前 "
"CR3 猜测其他任务。 初始栈、demand paging 与 COW 仍受地址空间资源限制和页面权限约束。"
msgstr ""
"Page tables, physical pages, the heap, and user-memory access are handled by"
" arch/x86_64/mm and the mm subdirectories according to their "
"responsibilities. User-pointer operations check ranges, permissions, "
"lengths, and target page tables; the current CR3 must not be used to guess "
"another task's address space. Initial stacks, demand paging, and COW remain "
"subject to address-space resource limits and page permissions."

msgid ""
"物理地址位宽按逻辑 CPU 缓存不可变的 CPUID 能力，包括“不支持”的结果， 避免用户缓冲区页表遍历时重复执行特征查询。该缓存不保存虚拟地址转换、"
" 直映射覆盖或页权限；这些检查仍读取当前页表。各 CPU 的缓存独立，首次查询 不分配内存、不获取锁，早期启动和 IRQ 路径也可使用。"
msgstr ""
"Physical address width is cached per logical CPU as an immutable CPUID "
"capability, including an unsupported result, to avoid repeating feature "
"queries during user-buffer page-table walks. This cache does not store "
"virtual-address translations, direct-map coverage, or page permissions; "
"those checks still read the current page tables. Each CPU's cache is "
"independent, and its first query neither allocates memory nor takes locks, "
"so it is usable during early boot and in IRQ paths."

msgid "缓存与引用"
msgstr "Caches and references"

msgid ""
"映射和仍被引用的文件页可超出空闲页缓存预算，保持共享映射一致性。 页缓存只把成功从 FAT32、ext 或 exFAT "
"普通文件完整加载、且从未授予共享写权限的 空闲页视为可丢弃；没有可证明磁盘来源的标识（包括当前无标志的 ISO 文件）、 tmpfs "
"和其他未知内容均不进入此路径。共享文件页在首次映射写权限或 ``mprotect`` 授予写权限之前永久降级为可能已修改。私有缓存映射写入走 "
"COW；撤销写权限不会 把可能已修改的页重新标记为 clean。目前没有普通文件 dirty 页完整写回，保留在 内存也不表示已经持久化到磁盘。"
msgstr ""
"Mapped file pages and file pages still referenced may exceed the idle page-"
"cache budget, preserving consistency of shared mappings. The page cache "
"considers only idle pages fully loaded successfully from FAT32, ext, or "
"exFAT regular files, and never granted shared write permission, to be "
"discardable. Entries without an identifier proving a disk source (including "
"currently unflagged ISO files), tmpfs, and other unknown contents are "
"excluded. Shared file pages are permanently downgraded to potentially "
"modified before first mapping with write permission or before ``mprotect`` "
"grants it. Writes to private cached mappings use COW; revoking write "
"permission does not mark potentially modified pages clean again. Full "
"writeback of regular-file dirty pages is not currently implemented, and "
"retention in memory does not mean data has been persisted to disk."

msgid ""
"``page_cache_reclaimable_pages`` 在缓存锁下提供瞬时页数快照；pin、put、失效与 "
"回收使用同一锁，后续并发变化可能使快照过期。``page_cache_reclaim`` 每次只摘除 无引用的可重读 clean 页，再在锁外归还其唯一"
" PMM 引用，按实际返回的数据页计数， 不调用 provider、分配堆或睡眠；为保证预算不被附带释放的元数据页超出，空的 overflow "
"元数据可保留复用。引用计数达到 ``UINT32_MAX`` 后永久 pinned，零引用的 额外 put "
"不会回绕。缓存未命中先确认可用槽，再在锁外分配和加载；发布前重检槽和 并发命中。加载失败保留原有条目；物理页耗尽时，已单独提交的 clean 回收可以在"
" 后续加载失败后仍生效，因为真实 backing 仍可重读。"
msgstr ""
"``page_cache_reclaimable_pages`` provides an instantaneous page-count "
"snapshot under the cache lock; pin, put, invalidation, and reclamation use "
"the same lock, and subsequent concurrent changes may make the snapshot "
"stale. Each ``page_cache_reclaim`` call removes only unreferenced, "
"rereadable clean pages, then returns their sole PMM reference outside the "
"lock. It counts data pages actually returned and does not call providers, "
"allocate heap memory, or sleep; empty overflow metadata may be retained for "
"reuse so incidental metadata-page releases do not exceed the budget. A "
"reference count reaching ``UINT32_MAX`` becomes permanently pinned, and an "
"extra put at zero references does not wrap. On a cache miss, an available "
"slot is confirmed before allocation and loading outside the lock; the slot "
"and concurrent hits are rechecked before publication. Load failure preserves"
" existing entries; when physical pages are exhausted, clean reclamation "
"already committed separately may remain effective even if the subsequent "
"load fails, because the real backing can still be reread."

msgid ""
"普通失效保留可能修改或来源未知的数据；文件终态销毁使用独立的 forget 操作撤销 旧 inode 的查找身份，仍被引用的旧帧在最后一次 put "
"后才释放。删除或替换一个名称 不等于 inode 销毁：ext 仅在最后链接的实际清理成功后 forget， 保留硬链接目标、同 inode "
"rename 空操作及仍持有引用的对象。 成功的 ext fallocate 普通分配保留已有修改，zero/punch "
"在磁盘操作成功后更新缓存内相交字节、保留边缘 外的数据；即使随后 inode 元数据读取失败，该缓存更新也已完成。执行所有权使文件 "
"fault、终态销毁与该操作串行；用户并发写仍可能与 range 操作竞态。ext provider 可能 "
"先提交若干子事务再返回错误，且不报告已完成子范围；这类失败保留缓存内容并返回 错误，不能保证磁盘回滚或未报告子范围的缓存一致性。"
msgstr ""
"Ordinary invalidation preserves potentially modified data and data of "
"unknown origin; final file destruction uses a separate forget operation to "
"revoke the old inode's lookup identity, with referenced old frames released "
"only after the final put. Deleting or replacing a name does not mean "
"destroying the inode: ext forgets only after actual cleanup of the last link"
" succeeds, preserving hard-link targets, same-inode rename no-ops, and "
"objects still referenced. Successful ordinary ext fallocate allocation "
"preserves existing modifications; after a successful disk operation, "
"zero/punch updates intersecting cached bytes and preserves data beyond the "
"edges. That cache update is already complete even if a subsequent inode "
"metadata read fails. Execution ownership serializes file faults, final "
"destruction, and this operation; concurrent user writes may still race with "
"range operations. An ext provider may commit some subtransactions before "
"returning an error and does not report completed subranges; such failures "
"preserve cache contents and return an error, without guaranteeing disk "
"rollback or cache consistency for unreported subranges."

msgid ""
"解绑、关闭或异常退出不能提前释放设备仍在使用的 backing。 字符设备映射在替换固定地址前先取得独立视图及每页缓存策略所有权；这一准入 "
"失败保留旧映射。设备页的策略由实际物理重叠关系约束，并用区间索引查找；部分 解除映射在撤销 PTE 和同步 TLB "
"后退休不再使用的页。一次操作移除同一视图的 多个拆分 VMA 时，最后 provider 回调仍受这些页的策略保护；其他页或 stage 的 "
"独立存活引用不会延长无关页的策略。实际 PAT/MTRR 与硬件行为仍需平台验证。 DRM retire "
"与维护队列的空提示只跳过确定无工作的锁路径；真实队列操作、 fence 和引用仍受原同步保护。"
msgstr ""
"Unbinding, close, or abnormal exit must not prematurely free backing still "
"in use by a device. Character-device mappings acquire ownership of an "
"independent view and per-page cache policy before replacing a fixed address;"
" failure of this admission preserves the old mapping. Device-page policies "
"are constrained by actual physical overlap and located through an interval "
"index; partial unmapping retires unused pages after revoking PTEs and "
"synchronizing TLBs. When one operation removes multiple split VMAs of the "
"same view, the final provider callback remains protected by those pages' "
"policies; independent live references to other pages or stages do not extend"
" unrelated pages' policies. Actual PAT/MTRR and hardware behavior still "
"require platform validation. Empty hints in DRM retire and maintenance "
"queues only skip lock paths known to have no work; real queue operations, "
"fences, and references retain their original synchronization."

msgid "内核堆"
msgstr "Kernel heap"

msgid ""
"``kernel_malloc`` 对 1–2048 字节请求使用 16、32、64、128、256、512、1024、 2048 字节的 "
"payload 尺寸类；页内独立元数据和对齐开销单独计入页面预算， 不会减少分配给对象的可用字节。较大请求持有连续物理页。所有返回的 payload "
"至少 16 字节对齐，并在每次分配时清零，包括复用的 slot；零大小、溢出和页耗尽 返回空指针。释放最后一个活 slot 时，空 slab "
"页面返还物理分配器。"
msgstr ""
"``kernel_malloc`` uses payload size classes of 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, "
"1024, and 2048 bytes for requests of 1–2048 bytes. Separate in-page metadata"
" and alignment overhead count separately against the page budget and do not "
"reduce the usable bytes allocated to objects. Larger requests hold "
"contiguous physical pages. All returned payloads are aligned to at least 16 "
"bytes and zeroed on every allocation, including reused slots; zero-size "
"requests, overflow, and page exhaustion return a null pointer. When the last"
" live slot is freed, the empty slab page is returned to the physical "
"allocator."

msgid ""
"堆仅以实际持有页面的地址索引识别 slab，slot 状态由页内独立位图记录；大对象 也只按实际持有的分配地址识别。持锁阶段不调用 "
"PMM、回收或清零：新页先在锁外 取得再发布，待释放的页先从索引摘除再在锁外返还。调用方仍须保证不访问已释放 "
"的对象，并避免释放过期指针；原始指针无法区分地址复用前后的不同对象。"
msgstr ""
"The heap identifies slabs only through an address index of pages it actually"
" holds, with slot state recorded in a separate in-page bitmap; large objects"
" are likewise identified only by actual held allocation addresses. PMM "
"calls, reclamation, and zeroing are not performed while holding the lock: "
"new pages are obtained outside the lock before publication, and pages to be "
"freed are removed from the index before being returned outside the lock. "
"Callers must still avoid accessing freed objects and freeing stale pointers;"
" raw pointers cannot distinguish different objects before and after address "
"reuse."

msgid "早期物理拓扑和 bootstrap"
msgstr "Early physical topology and bootstrap"

msgid ""
"``mm_topology_workspace_size`` 校验借用的固件地图、启动块及对象范围，计算 "
"调用方所需的工作区；``mm_topology_build`` 不分配内存，把规范化结果写入该 工作区，并仅在成功时发布视图。工作区须 8 "
"字节对齐、不与输入或输出重叠， 其生命周期须覆盖所有视图消费者；地图、字符串和其他启动块只借用到构建完成。 "
"``mm_topology_destroy`` 只撤销视图，不释放工作区。固件块及入口必须在调用前 完整可读，地址不是对任意物理地址安全解引用的承诺。"
msgstr ""
"``mm_topology_workspace_size`` validates borrowed firmware maps, boot "
"blocks, and object ranges and computes the workspace required by the caller;"
" ``mm_topology_build`` allocates no memory, writes normalized results into "
"that workspace, and publishes a view only on success. The workspace must be "
"8-byte aligned, must not overlap input or output, and must outlive all view "
"consumers; maps, strings, and other boot blocks are borrowed only until "
"construction completes. ``mm_topology_destroy`` only revokes the view and "
"does not free the workspace. Firmware blocks and entries must be fully "
"readable before the call; an address does not promise that an arbitrary "
"physical address can be safely dereferenced."

msgid ""
"先合并 usable 字节区间，再按 4 KiB 页向内取完整 usable 页；保留向外取整， 对冲突采用固件保留优先；EFI 最终 "
"地图存在时优先使用其可用声明，较早的 Multiboot 保留声明仍能排除重叠页面。 EFI Loader/Boot Services、ACPI "
"reclaim 以及 EFI runtime 内存不会被当作当前可 分配页。视图中保留 RAM 仍携带 RAM "
"标记；``total_ram_bytes`` 是物理上界内经 确认的完整 RAM 页总量，包括这些保留页，不包括固件冲突页，也不是运行 PMM 的 "
"MemTotal。``physical_limit`` 为 ``min(2^physical_bits, 64 TiB)``，输入位宽 只接受 "
"32..52；``clipped_descriptors`` 记录越过该上界的固件描述符数，不对 缺失地图猜测 "
"RAM。范围和工作区大小由描述符数量决定，稀疏高物理地址不会导致 按最大 PFN 分配元数据。"
msgstr ""
"Usable byte ranges are merged first, then rounded inward to complete usable "
"4 KiB pages; reservations are rounded outward, and firmware reservations "
"take precedence in conflicts. When a final EFI map exists, its usable "
"declarations are preferred, but earlier Multiboot reservations can still "
"exclude overlapping pages. EFI Loader/Boot Services, ACPI reclaim, and EFI "
"runtime memory are not treated as currently allocatable pages. Reserved RAM "
"in the view retains its RAM flag; ``total_ram_bytes`` is the total confirmed"
" complete RAM pages within the physical bound, including these reserved "
"pages but excluding firmware-conflict pages, and is not the running PMM's "
"MemTotal. ``physical_limit`` is ``min(2^physical_bits, 64 TiB)``, accepting "
"only input widths 32..52; ``clipped_descriptors`` records the number of "
"firmware descriptors crossing this bound, and RAM is not guessed when maps "
"are missing. Range and workspace sizes depend on descriptor count; sparse "
"high physical addresses do not cause metadata allocation proportional to the"
" maximum PFN."

msgid ""
"拓扑保护低 1 MiB、128–192 MiB 内核孔（覆盖当前内核、启动栈及静态页表）、 借用的启动信息/地图、模块、已知 framebuffer 与"
" EFI 系统表所在页。实际绑定 framebuffer 的两个物理预留区由 bootstrap 另外覆盖。调用方必须先建立现有共享 "
"identity/direct map、完成 framebuffer 初始化且尚未启动 PMM，在 BSP 关中断的 启动上下文调用 "
"``mm_bootstrap_prepare``；它先确认所有借用输入的完整范围可达， 再直接扫描原始地图与全部保留，在不分配内存的条件下合并相邻及重叠"
" usable 字节覆盖，从当前映射内选出无冲突的页对齐工作区，最后调用纯拓扑构建器并将 工作区标记为 bootstrap 持有。"
msgstr ""
"The topology protects the low 1 MiB, the 128–192 MiB kernel hole (covering "
"the current kernel, boot stack, and static page tables), borrowed boot "
"information/maps, modules, known framebuffers, and pages containing the EFI "
"system table. Bootstrap additionally covers the two physical reservations "
"for the actually bound framebuffer. The caller must first establish the "
"existing shared identity/direct map and complete framebuffer initialization,"
" then call ``mm_bootstrap_prepare`` in BSP boot context with interrupts "
"disabled and before PMM startup. It first confirms that the full ranges of "
"all borrowed inputs are reachable, then directly scans the raw map and all "
"reservations, merges adjacent and overlapping usable byte coverage without "
"allocating memory, selects a conflict-free page-aligned workspace within "
"current mappings, and finally calls the pure topology builder and marks the "
"workspace as bootstrap-owned."

msgid ""
"工作区按描述符及启动对象个数为扫描事件分配两条边界，并为范围与后续分割预留 ``4 * (地图描述符数 + 模块数 + 10) + 16`` "
"个条目；任一容量不足都明确失败。 每次 ``mm_bootstrap_alloc`` 只取得一个可用范围的连续前缀，核对完整页串是否 满足 "
"inclusive mask 和当前共享映射，并合并相邻的 bootstrap 所有页；它不调用 "
"PMM、堆或回收。``mm_bootstrap_finish`` 只关闭分配，不释放工作区或任何已分配 页；后续元数据和页表消费者必须继承这些预留。"
msgstr ""
"The workspace allocates two boundaries per scan event according to the "
"number of descriptors and boot objects and reserves ``4 * (地图描述符数 + 模块数 + "
"10) + 16`` entries for ranges and subsequent splits; any capacity shortage "
"fails explicitly. Each ``mm_bootstrap_alloc`` obtains only a contiguous "
"prefix of one usable range, checks the entire page run against the inclusive"
" mask and current shared mappings, and merges adjacent bootstrap-owned "
"pages; it does not call the PMM, heap, or reclamation. "
"``mm_bootstrap_finish`` only closes allocation and does not free the "
"workspace or any allocated pages; later metadata and page-table consumers "
"must inherit these reservations."

msgid "运行时物理页分配"
msgstr "Runtime physical-page allocation"

msgid ""
"``mm_init`` 在现有共享 direct map 与 framebuffer 准备完成后，以实际 CPUID 物理地址位宽准备 "
"bootstrap 拓扑。``mm_runtime_init`` 只接受已发布的 bootstrap 视图，在释放任何页面之前为每个已映射的可信 RAM"
" 段预留分段位图和引用计数； 元数据成本随这些 RAM 页数与段数增长，不随稀疏空洞的最高 PFN 增长。预留可能 "
"修改拓扑范围，计量与最终可用页播种是两个独立阶段；失败时页面不发布，已经 取得的 bootstrap "
"页仍保留。缺失或不可信地图不会触发猜测的备用内存范围，``mm_init`` 会停止启动。"
msgstr ""
"After the existing shared direct map and framebuffer are ready, ``mm_init`` "
"prepares bootstrap topology using the actual CPUID physical-address width. "
"``mm_runtime_init`` accepts only a published bootstrap view and reserves "
"segmented bitmaps and reference counts for each mapped trusted RAM segment "
"before freeing any pages. Metadata cost grows with those RAM pages and "
"segments, not with the highest PFN across sparse holes. Reservations may "
"modify topology ranges, so accounting and final seeding of available pages "
"are separate phases; on failure, no pages are published and bootstrap pages "
"already acquired remain reserved. A missing or untrusted map does not "
"trigger a guessed fallback memory range; ``mm_init`` stops boot."

msgid ""
"运行 PMM 只管理当前实际共享映射覆盖的可信 RAM。启动时的临时低地址映射用于 取得早期页表；运行时按拓扑稀疏建立直映射，而不是只保留 16 GiB"
" 前缀。 64 TiB 是虚拟窗口的设计上界，不能当作已经验证的 RAM 容量。 ``mm_phys_is_ram`` "
"从冻结的可信拓扑查询完整字节范围，包含保留及当前尚未 映射的可信 RAM，且不建立映射或转移引用；``mm_page_refcount`` "
"快照不获取引用。调用方持有引用时才可 retain，计数 饱和后页面保持 pinned，重复 free 不会增加空闲容量。普通分配优先使用 4 GiB "
"以上的高地址并向低地址寻找连续页面；DMA 限制检查分配串最后一个字节。持锁 阶段不分配、睡眠或回收，页面声明成功后在锁外清零再返回。页表和 PMM "
"元数据 占用实际 RAM；具体容量、启动拓扑和性能须在目标环境分别验证。"
msgstr ""
"The running PMM manages only trusted RAM covered by actual current shared "
"mappings. Temporary low-address boot mappings are used to obtain early page "
"tables; at runtime the direct map is built sparsely according to topology "
"rather than retaining only a 16 GiB prefix. 64 TiB is the virtual window's "
"design limit and must not be treated as a validated RAM capacity. "
"``mm_phys_is_ram`` queries full byte ranges in the frozen trusted topology, "
"including reserved and currently unmapped trusted RAM, without establishing "
"mappings or transferring references; a ``mm_page_refcount`` snapshot does "
"not acquire a reference. Callers may retain only while holding a reference; "
"pages remain pinned once the counter saturates, and repeated free does not "
"increase free capacity. Ordinary allocation prefers high addresses above 4 "
"GiB and searches downward for contiguous pages; DMA constraints check the "
"final byte of the allocation run. No allocation, sleeping, or reclamation "
"occurs while holding the lock; after pages are successfully claimed, they "
"are zeroed outside the lock before return. Page tables and PMM metadata "
"consume actual RAM; specific capacities, boot topology, and performance must"
" be validated separately in the target environment."

msgid "用户地址空间的丢弃和锁定"
msgstr "Discarding and locking user address spaces"

msgid ""
"``MADV_DONTNEED`` 按页处理现有用户映射：私有匿名页（包括 fork 后的 COW 副本） "
"重新访问时从零页开始；文件页重新从原文件或缓存取得。共享匿名页由 MM 私有的 RAM backing 对象保持，fork "
"的不同地址空间持有同一对象；SysV 共享页由原 segment 持有，tmpfs 由 inode 持有。丢弃只撤销调用地址空间的 "
"PTE，仍有其他引用的共享数据 不会因此消失。跨空洞的范围仍处理存在的映射并返回 ``ENOMEM``；锁定页及设备映射 返回 "
"``EINVAL``。每批 PTE 撤销后先同步远端用户 TLB，再释放该批 PTE 的物理页或 缓存引用。``MADV_FREE`` 尚未实现，返回 "
"``EOPNOTSUPP``，不会被当作立即清零。"
msgstr ""
"``MADV_DONTNEED`` processes existing user mappings page by page: private "
"anonymous pages (including post-fork COW copies) restart from zero-filled "
"pages on next access; file pages are obtained again from the original file "
"or cache. Shared anonymous pages are retained by MM-private RAM backing "
"objects shared by the different address spaces after fork; SysV shared pages"
" are retained by their original segments, and tmpfs pages by their inodes. "
"Discard revokes only the calling address space's PTEs, so shared data with "
"other references does not disappear. Ranges crossing holes still process "
"existing mappings and return ``ENOMEM``; locked pages and device mappings "
"return ``EINVAL``. After each batch of PTE revocations, remote user TLBs are"
" synchronized before releasing that batch's physical-page or cache "
"references. ``MADV_FREE`` is not yet implemented and returns ``EOPNOTSUPP``;"
" it is not treated as immediate zeroing."

msgid ""
"``mincore`` 同时考虑有 backing 的普通和 ``PROT_NONE`` PTE，以及仍驻留的文件缓存、 tmpfs、SysV "
"和共享匿名 backing；没有 PTE 不等同于文件或共享 backing 不在 RAM。 "
"返回值是瞬时快照，不固定后续驻留状态。共享匿名页按对象页号使用固定深度基数树； 每个 MM 的虚址范围和每个对象的 backing "
"范围使用平衡区间索引。部分移除只检查 被移除范围的已驻留页及其幸存引用，不逐页扫描全局 MM 注册表。"
msgstr ""
"``mincore`` considers both ordinary backed PTEs and backed ``PROT_NONE`` "
"PTEs, as well as resident file cache, tmpfs, SysV, and shared anonymous "
"backing; absence of a PTE does not mean file or shared backing is absent "
"from RAM. The result is an instantaneous snapshot and does not pin "
"subsequent residency. Shared anonymous pages use a fixed-depth radix tree "
"indexed by object page number; virtual-address ranges per MM and backing "
"ranges per object use balanced interval indexes. Partial removal examines "
"only resident pages in the removed range and their surviving references, "
"without scanning the global MM registry page by page."

msgid ""
"``mlock`` 按 Linux 规则覆盖未对齐端点所在的整页；部分范围按 VMA 切分并保留 文件、设备和 SysV backing "
"引用；不允许拆分的设备映射拒绝部分锁定或解锁。 普通锁定在成功前预故障，``ONFAULT`` 延迟分配但仍占用完整范围的 "
"``RLIMIT_MEMLOCK`` 配额；有效 ``CAP_IPC_LOCK`` 可越过配额。 ``MCL_CURRENT`` "
"包含原始隐式栈，``MCL_FUTURE`` 随共享 MM 应用于新映射、brk 和 栈增长；已显式解锁的既有栈页重新 fault "
"不会自动再次锁定。独立 fork 不继承锁， 共享 MM 线程共享锁定状态，包含不同线程栈的 peer 对原始栈的重访；exec 的新地址 "
"空间从空策略开始。``MCL_CURRENT``、``MCL_FUTURE`` 新映射和已锁映射的 mremap "
"在配额及元数据准入后尽力预故障，不可访问的 guard 或物理页分配失败不伪造驻留页。 普通 ``mlock`` 的预故障失败仍会返回错误。 "
"预故障按最多 32 次 VMA 槽位检查或页处理让出外层执行事务，重新取得事务后重新 解析 MM 身份和映射；不可访问的 VMA "
"整段跳过，单个范围分配或后端失败后继续检查 其他独立映射。最佳努力遍历按槽位而非虚址排序；同一 MM 的映射元数据或已驻留 PTE "
"被撤销时重新检查，其他 MM 的活动不会重置进度。普通 ``mlock`` 先检查全部页， "
"再重新核对配额、覆盖范围和切分资源，最后一次发布锁策略；失败不会改变已有锁。 预故障期间的私有临时范围不占锁配额；换出候选检查会避开这些范围。 "
"批次之间可处理本 CPU 中断并允许其他 CPU 获得执行事务；当前内核不能在该 Ring 0 调用中切换本 CPU 到其他用户任务，因此这不保证单 "
"CPU 的任务调度延迟。"
msgstr ""
"``mlock`` follows Linux rules by covering entire pages containing unaligned "
"endpoints; partial ranges split VMAs while retaining file, device, and SysV "
"backing references, and device mappings that prohibit splitting reject "
"partial locking or unlocking. Ordinary locking prefaults before success; "
"``ONFAULT`` defers allocation but still consumes ``RLIMIT_MEMLOCK`` quota "
"for the entire range, while effective ``CAP_IPC_LOCK`` can exceed the quota."
" ``MCL_CURRENT`` includes the original implicit stack, and ``MCL_FUTURE`` "
"applies through shared MM to new mappings, brk, and stack growth; refaulting"
" existing stack pages that were explicitly unlocked does not automatically "
"relock them. Independent fork does not inherit locks; shared-MM threads "
"share lock state, including peer revisits to the original stack with "
"different thread stacks, and a new exec address space starts with an empty "
"policy. ``MCL_CURRENT``, new ``MCL_FUTURE`` mappings, and mremap of locked "
"mappings prefault on a best-effort basis after quota and metadata admission,"
" without fabricating resident pages for inaccessible guards or failed "
"physical-page allocations. Prefault failure for ordinary ``mlock`` still "
"returns an error. Prefaulting yields the outer execution transaction after "
"at most 32 VMA-slot checks or page operations, then resolves MM identity and"
" mappings again after reacquiring it; inaccessible VMAs are skipped in full,"
" and allocation or backend failure in one range does not stop checks of "
"other independent mappings. Best-effort traversal follows slot order rather "
"than virtual-address order; revoking mapping metadata or resident PTEs in "
"the same MM triggers rechecking, while activity in other MMs does not reset "
"progress. Ordinary ``mlock`` checks all pages first, then rechecks quota, "
"coverage, and splitting resources, and publishes the lock policy once at the"
" end; failure leaves existing locks unchanged. Private temporary ranges "
"during prefaulting consume no lock quota and are avoided when checking swap-"
"out candidates. Between batches, this CPU's interrupts can be handled and "
"other CPUs can acquire execution transactions; the current kernel cannot "
"switch this CPU to another user task within this Ring 0 call, so this does "
"not guarantee single-CPU task scheduling latency."

msgid ""
"锁策略和共享匿名 backing 归属以物理 CR3 根及私有 generation 标识；销毁根时先 "
"撤销该身份，避免根帧复用后继承旧状态。generation 可供后续 MM 服务使用，不改变 公开 task 或 address_space "
"布局。内存压力路径可回收可证明干净、可重读的 缓存页，并将满足独占条件的私有匿名页写入已启用的 swap；其条件、恢复及 OOM 边界见 "
":doc:`../admin-guide/swap`。并非所有 backing 都可换出，换页与硬件能力 也需要通过目标环境的实际运行结果分别确认。"
msgstr ""
"Lock policies and shared anonymous backing ownership are identified by the "
"physical CR3 root and a private generation; root destruction revokes that "
"identity first to prevent reused root frames from inheriting old state. The "
"generation is available to later MM services without changing public task or"
" address_space layouts. Memory-pressure paths can reclaim provably clean, "
"rereadable cache pages and write eligible exclusively owned private "
"anonymous pages to enabled swap; see :doc:`../admin-guide/swap` for "
"conditions, recovery, and OOM boundaries. Not all backing is swappable, and "
"paging and hardware capabilities must also be confirmed separately through "
"actual runs in the target environment."
